undaries. | ['subtree:network-architect', 'anti-cheat-integrity', 'platform-services', 'destruction-fracture', 'persistence-save', 'packaging-release-patching', 'character-movement', 'online-services-liveops', 'narrative-dialogue']\nK-TOOLS | Production tooling and content workflows: editor, pipeline, collaboration, iteration speed. | ['subtree:editor-architect', 'subtree:content-pipeline-architect', 'hot-reload-iteration', 'developer-experience-docs', 'ui-architect', 'terrain', 'procedural-generation', 'cinematics-sequencer', 'scripting-runtime', 'world-data-model', 'subtree:build-release-architect', 'owns-area:TOOL', 'kind:tool']\nK-PLATFORM | Hardware, operating systems, consoles, graphics APIs, packaging and platform requirements. | ['subtree:platform-architect', 'rhi-core', 'subtree:build-release-architect', 'certification-compliance', 'async-io-storage', 'crash-diagnostics', 'rhi-d3d12', 'rhi-vulkan', 'rhi-metal', 'rhi-webgpu']\nK-PERF | Scalability bottlenecks: serialization points, excess synchronization, cache inefficiency, GPU stalls, bandwidth, poor asymptotics. | ['all', 'subtree:performance-architect', 'subtree:world-architect', 'runtime-scalability']\nK-PROD | Could a real team ship games with this: workflows, content scale, team scale, schedules, live operations. | ['all', 'tier:orchestrator', 'developer-experience-docs', 'subtree:build-release-architect', 'engine-product-management', 'reference-games']\nK-FUTURE | Does the architecture block likely next-5-year technologies: neural rendering, work graphs, cluster RT, ML animation, new storage and memory, new plat | ['all']\nK-COMPLETE | Exactly one responsibility: find engine capabilities or engineering disciplines that are missing. | ['all']\nK-LEGACY | Find accidental legacy architecture: central sequential update loops, deep inheritance, global state, hot-path virtual dispatch, CPU-driven rendering, | ['all']\nK-GAMEPLAY | Animation, audio, AI, gameplay framework, UI, text, localization and accessi